NNAAMMEE
     hhiiddqquuiirrkk — HID quirks module

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this module into the kernel, place the following line in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee hhiidd

     Alternatively, to load the module at boot time, place the following line
     in loader.conf(5):

           hidquirk_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The hhiiddqquuiirrkk module provides support for adding quirks for HID devices

     HQ_HID_IGNORE
             device should be ignored by hid class

     HQ_KBD_BOOTPROTO
             device should set the boot protocol

     HQ_MS_BOOTPROTO
             device should set the boot protocol

     HQ_MS_BAD_CLASS
             doesn't identify properly

     HQ_MS_LEADING_BYTE
             mouse sends an unknown leading byte

     HQ_MS_REVZ
             mouse has Z-axis reversed

     HQ_MS_VENDOR_BTN
             mouse has buttons in vendor usage page

     HQ_SPUR_BUT_UP
             spurious mouse button up events

     HQ_MT_TIMESTAMP
             Multitouch device exports HW timestamps 0x1b5a01

     See _/_s_y_s_/_d_e_v_/_h_i_d_/_h_i_d_q_u_i_r_k_._h for the complete list of supported quirks.

LLOOAADDEERR TTUUNNAABBLLEE
     The following tunable can be set at the loader(8) prompt before booting
     the kernel, or stored in loader.conf(5).

     _h_w_._h_i_d_._q_u_i_r_k_._%_d
             The value is a string whose format is:

                   "BusId VendorId ProductId LowRevision HighRevision HQ_QUIRK,..."

             Installs the quirks HHQQ__QQUUIIRRKK,,...... for all HID devices matching
             BBuussIIdd and VVeennddoorrIIdd and PPrroodduuccttIIdd which have a hardware revision
             between and including LLoowwRReevviissiioonn and HHiigghhRReevviissiioonn.

             BBuussIIdd, VVeennddoorrIIdd, PPrroodduuccttIIdd, LLoowwRReevviissiioonn and HHiigghhRReevviissiioonn are all
             16 bits numbers which can be decimal or hexadecimal based.

             A maximum of 100 variables hhww..hhiidd..qquuiirrkk..00,, ..11,, ......,, ..9999 can be
             defined.

             If a matching entry is found in the kernel's internal quirks ta‐
             ble, it is replaced by the new definition.

             Else a new entry is created given that the quirk table is not
             full.

             The kernel iterates over the hhww..hhiidd..qquuiirrkk..NN variables starting at
             NN == 00 and stops at NN == 9999 or the first non-existing one.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     To install a quirk at boot time, place one or several lines like the fol‐
     lowing in loader.conf(5):

           hw.hid.quirk.0="0x18 0x6cb 0x1941 0 0xffff HQ_MT_TIMESTAMP"

